  "id": "velkspreownedfurnishings",
  "neon": "#ff8a4a",
  "note": "VELK'S PRE-OWNED FURNISHINGS — the second-hand furniture warehouse on Ironside Street.\n\nThe hoist is the design. A furniture warehouse is a building you get a wardrobe out of, so it has a\nloading door on the first floor, a beam over it and a shutter under it. The arm drew it as a junk\nshop with a window.\n\nThe big sign is on the flank. A gable end is where a city puts its largest advertisement, and the\nfront of this building is mostly door.\n\nThe tile's prose: the shop has outgrown itself and spilled onto the grass. A wardrobe and four\ndining chairs stand out front under a tarpaulin that covers about half of them, and a board\nleaning on the shop front says EVERYTHING IN HERE OUTLIVED SOMEBODY. They are detail parts, not\nmass: the pavement is past the plot line, where `segFit` would trim a box. The name is on the\nfascia, so the board carries only the second line.\n\nThe front is a warehouse elevation in two tones: brick piers at the corners and either side of the\nloading bay over a darker infill, a string course at the first floor, and a corbelled cornice. The\nupper windows are few and dirty, three small openings, and nothing behind them is lit.",
  "pal": "ty_signalbox",
  "replaces": "junkshop",
